        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "t4PFm",
          "name": "Handoff Notes",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 24,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "rEDU4",
              "name": "Notes Row 1",
              "gap": 24,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "note",
                  "id": "hIxH6",
                  "name": "Note Flow",
                  "width": 380,
                  "height": 447,
                  "content": "S13 PILIH BENGKEL — FLOW\nEntry: S11 'Lanjut' (draft with 1–5 units). Card tap → S14 (push). In-flow S14 CTA 'Pilih bengkel ini' commits the workshop and goes to S15; if the viewed workshop is already chosen the CTA reads 'Lanjut ke jadwal'. A workshop carried in from standalone S14 skips S13 (S11 → S15). 'Ubah' on S15 / S16 comes back here with the chosen card tagged 'Dipilih'. No footer on S13: the choice is committed from S14. Back → S11 (draft kept); close → the booking-exit dialog, only with 1+ selection ('Simpan & keluar' / 'Lanjutkan booking'). Standalone S14 (back only, CTA 'Booking di sini' → S10 with the workshop carried) is opened from the workshop row of S18 / S20 (steps 11 / 16)."
                },
                {
                  "type": "note",
                  "id": "AIJ8h",
                  "name": "Note List Detail",
                  "width": 380,
                  "height": 470,
                  "content": "LIST-DETAIL (EXPANDED / LARGE)\nExpanded 1024: list 400 + pane 552. Large 1280: list 440 + pane 768. The pane shows S14 content (WorkshopDetailContent), scrolls on its own, CTA pinned at the pane bottom. Tapping a card only PREVIEWS it (border-accent, no check mark); the pane CTA commits. 'Dipilih' = the committed workshop and can differ from the previewed card. First state: the chosen workshop, else the nearest card. Medium (800 portrait) has no pane: a tap pushes S14 (stacked, max 720). List scroll position and selection survive rotation. The heading + helper drop out of the two-pane layouts (stepper, search and chips carry the context); the list and the pane scroll independently, and the stepper stays centered at 720."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "foimQ",
              "name": "Notes Row 2",
              "gap": 24,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "note",
                  "id": "ZGudL",
                  "name": "Note Filters",
                  "width": 380,
                  "height": 465,
                  "content": "FILTERS AND SORT\n'Buka sekarang' = independent toggle. 'Terdekat' / 'Rating tertinggi' = mutually exclusive sort, one always on, default Terdekat; off sort chips carry a sort icon and the 'Urutkan' caption groups them. Result line '5 bengkel · urut terdekat' is a polite live region. 'Buka sekarang' looks at the current time only: a workshop closed now stays bookable ('Tutup · buka 08.00', tappable; the S14 CTA is enabled with a helper line), because S15 slots run 08.00–16.00 for D+0…D+14. Search matches name and area; clear = Semantics 'Hapus pencarian'. The chip row scrolls horizontally; the 24 dp fade cue shows wherever it overflows (phone, list columns 400 / 440) and is off where it fits (720)."
                },
                {
                  "type": "note",
                  "id": "JI8Dw",
                  "name": "Note Estimate",
                  "width": 380,
                  "height": 380,
                  "content": "ESTIMATE PER WORKSHOP\n'Estimasi N jam untuk M motor' = makespan of the draft's units over that workshop's bays (60 min each: 1 bay 3 jam, 2 bays 2 jam, 3 bays 1 jam), computed in the domain layer. S11 shows its duration for a standard 2-bay workshop because no workshop is chosen yet ('asumsi bengkel 2 bay'); S16 shows the final figure. Prices stay 'Estimasi' and are uniform across workshops. The hour figure uses tabular figures (FontFeature.tabularFigures) so it does not shift when the unit count changes. The chosen workshop shows the 'Dipilih' tag on S13 and on its S14 (status row); its CTA reads 'Lanjut ke jadwal'."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "OgHlw",
              "name": "Notes Row 3",
              "gap": 24,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "note",
                  "id": "B9x0K",
                  "name": "Note Map",
                  "width": 380,
                  "height": 400,
                  "content": "STATIC MAP AND MAPS INTENT\nThe map is an asset (8–10 ship with the app), no API key, no map SDK. StaticMap is drawn from theme tokens here so it flips in dark mode; the Flutter asset is a similar image per workshop. 'Buka di Maps' opens an external intent via url_launcher. The photo slot is a 16:9 aspect-ratio box (gradient + storefront + initials), the same recipe as the 80x80 card thumb, so layout never jumps when a photo is missing. 'Salin' copies the address (snackbar 'Alamat disalin'). The map is an informative image: Semantics(image: true, label: 'Peta lokasi Bengkel Jaya Motor, Jl. Melati Raya'); 'Buka di Maps' is its action."
                },
                {
                  "type": "note",
                  "id": "axN9d",
                  "name": "Note Semantics",
                  "width": 380,
                  "height": 500,
                  "content": "SEMANTICS, FOCUS, MOTION\nCard: 'Bengkel Jaya Motor, bintang 4,8, 1,2 kilometer, buka sampai 17.00, 2 bay, estimasi 2 jam untuk 3 motor, dipilih'; closed: '…, tutup, buka pukul 08.00'. Back 'Kembali', close 'Tutup booking'. Focus order: back → close → stepper → search → clear → chips → cards in reading order; tablet: list, then pane content, then the pane CTA. Skeleton shimmer 150–250 ms loop, static under reduce-motion (MediaQuery.disableAnimations). Open / closed / chosen always have icon + text. Chips are 32 dp inside a 48 dp target. Card name: max 2 lines, then an ellipsis; the full name is in the Semantics label and wraps on S14. List-detail keyboard: Enter / Space on a card previews it (focus stays in the list), Tab moves on to the pane."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
