    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "WaJs1",
      "x": 3520,
      "y": 55598,
      "name": "S18 Handoff Notes · Phone",
      "height": 426,
      "gap": 24,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "note",
          "id": "ViJuJ",
          "name": "S18 Note · Success and motion",
          "width": 380,
          "height": 384,
          "content": "SUCCESS AND MOTION\nEntrance, once per visit (infrequent, so staged): the check badge enters with scale 0.25 → 1, opacity 0 → 1 and blur 4 px → 0 (spring, duration 300 ms, bounce 0; Flutter: ScaleTransition + FadeTransition on Curves.easeOutCubic, blur optional); title, subline and ticket follow, staggered by about 100 ms. With MediaQuery.disableAnimations everything appears at once, with no scale, blur or stagger. A polite live region announces \"Booking berhasil\" once. The state is carried by the check icon and the words, not by green alone. No generated art."
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "id": "fDF1S",
          "name": "S18 Note · Ticket and QR",
          "width": 380,
          "height": 384,
          "content": "TICKET AND QR\nThe ticket is announced as one group: \"Tiket booking TS-260929-0417, 3 motor, Bengkel Jaya Motor, Selasa 29 September pukul 09.00, total estimasi Rp385.200, bayar di bengkel\". The QR encodes the booking code only (qr_flutter, 126 dp code on a 176 dp white tile, 4-module quiet zone) and stays dark-on-light in dark mode, never themed; text alternative \"Kode QR untuk TS-260929-0417\". The code appears once, here; Salin (48 dp, \"Salin kode booking\") copies it and shows the snackbar \"Kode booking disalin\". The matrix in the design is a real, decodable QR."
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "id": "SLnGC",
          "name": "S18 Note · Actions and navigation",
          "width": 380,
          "height": 426,
          "content": "ACTIONS AND NAVIGATION\nNo app bar. Flat sticky footer (0 glass): \"Lacak status\" → S20, \"Kembali ke beranda\" → S05. System back = Beranda; the draft is cleared on success (route /booking/success/:bookingId), so the flow cannot be re-entered. Loading: caption \"Membuat tiket…\" (polite live region), static skeleton under reduce motion, \"Lacak status\" disabled with \"Tiket sedang dibuat\". Focus order: initial semantics focus on the title \"Booking berhasil!\", then Salin, (P2: Bagikan tiket, Tambah ke kalender), Lacak status, Kembali ke beranda; the read-only status rows on Tablet-L are skipped. Unit rows summarize services; the full list lives on S21."
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "id": "ZU3e9",
          "name": "S18 Note · Unit rows and split",
          "width": 380,
          "height": 300,
          "content": "UNIT ROWS AND SPLIT\nRow = motor name + \"Unit -A · service summary\" (max 2 lines, then ellipsis; wraps under the badge at ×1.3) + badge \"Terjadwal\" (icon + text). Split schedule: a slot line per row and the recap reads \"Sel, 29 Sep 2026 · jam berbeda tiap motor\". A single motor keeps one row (-A) and total Rp85.000 (no voucher applies). The total is an estimate; the voucher line lives on S16 and S23."
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "id": "RztLg",
          "name": "S18 Note · P2 and stress",
          "width": 380,
          "height": 321,
          "content": "P2 AND STRESS\nP2 variant: \"Bagikan tiket\" (OS share sheet: code + QR image) and \"Tambah ke kalender\" (calendar intent for the arrival slot), stacked into two rows under text ×1.3 (Flutter Wrap). The 5-unit specimen is \"Demo: 5 motor\": TS-261002-0418, Jum 2 Okt 2026 · 08.00 (a 5-motor shared slot needs an empty hour) and scrolls under the footer at 360×640. Text ×1.3 wraps the 54-character workshop name to three lines, nothing clips."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "a82BUy",
      "x": 10556,
      "y": 55598,
      "name": "S18 Handoff Notes · Tablet-Portrait",
      "gap": 24,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "note",
          "id": "YMS29",
          "name": "S18 Note · Layout",
          "width": 380,
          "height": 300,
          "content": "LAYOUT\nTicket centered, max width 560 (TicketCard Phone stretched: tear lines 560, right notch at 548). The action bar is a full-width surface strip with a 560 dp inner column, pinned to the viewport bottom; there is no app bar, status bar or gesture bar in a fixed tablet viewport."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "jBlvc",
      "x": 15496,
      "y": 55598,
      "name": "S18 Handoff Notes · Tablet-Landscape",
      "gap": 24,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "note",
          "id": "RMbyV",
          "name": "S18 Note · Layout",
          "width": 380,
          "height": 300,
          "content": "LAYOUT\nGroup 480 + 24 + 400 = 904 dp, centered. Left: SuccessHeader + TicketCard Landscape (QR, code, recap); right: read-only status panel (rows carry no chevron; S20 owns unit navigation) and the pane variant of the actions. The same composition holds at Expanded 1024 (904 fits), so there is no separate Expanded frame."
        }
      ]
    },
